1	// The precondition engine (task-preconditions DESIGN): may THIS task run now? A
2	// task declares `preconditions` — a list of named conditions — and this module
3	// turns that declaration plus the collected signals into a verdict. Sibling of
4	// merge-policy.mjs beside it, and deliberately its mirror image in two ways:
5	//
6	//   THE LIST IS A CONJUNCTION. `['X', 'Y || Z']` is `X && (Y || Z)`. An automerge
7	//   policy GRANTS, so its comma is a union; preconditions REQUIRE, so the comma
8	//   is `&&` and `||` lives inside one entry. Each field then reads against its
9	//   own English.
10	//
11	//   IT FAILS LOUD, NOT CLOSED. An unresolvable merge policy authorizes nothing,
12	//   which parks a PR in front of a person. An unresolvable precondition that
13	//   declined would be permanent, silent staleness — nothing goes red when a task
14	//   stops running — so an unknown term, a malformed argument or an unreadable
15	//   signal returns `{ error }`, a failed run in the queue's failure lane.
16	//
17	// THE EXPRESSION IS THE WHOLE OF "WHEN" (tasks-dispatch DESIGN §5). The engine
18	// keeps no calendar: every scheduler tick asks every task, and the cadence a task
19	// keeps is one of its own conditions, read off its own run history — `due:<cadence>`,
20	// `last-run-over:<duration>`, `woken` — beside whatever else it requires. `none`
21	// is therefore retired: a task with no condition at all would run at every tick.
22	//
23	// THE VOCABULARY HAS TWO HOMES. The built-ins below are the run-history, movement
24	// and pending-PR conditions every repo shares. A task whose gate is its own ships a
25	// `preconditions.mjs` beside its `task.json` exporting `terms`, resolved after the
26	// built-ins in one flat namespace where a collision is loud — so the declaration
27	// and the gate it names are one directory apart.
28	//
29	// Import-light and pure over the signals: no I/O, so the same evaluation runs at
30	// the scheduler's tick and at the executor's pick.
31	
32	import { anchorInstant, CADENCES, DUE_TERM, ELAPSED_TERM, NOT_FAILED_TERM, WOKEN_TERM, parseDuration } from './calendar.mjs';
